# Entity single source of truth

`AGENTS.md` and `docs/design.md` are authoritative. Entity definitions generate
persistence metadata, GraphQL CRUD, nested relations, policies and change events.

- Ordinary persisted reads use generated GraphQL roots/relations or existing
  typed entity-layer query abstractions. Trusted repository reads do not apply
  the public caller's ownership policy: establish authorized scope first.
- Domain service/job/action writes use generated mutations through
  `execute_mutation` or generated resolvers. Related invariant writes use the
  originating typed `MutationContext`, preserving rollback, hooks and events.
- No application domain SQL. Bulk work, joins and aggregates are not exceptions;
  extend the generated entity layer when a typed capability is missing.
- Private auth storage, schema/bootstrap, logging ingestion and managed-object
  infrastructure require narrow documented trusted boundaries. Database-backed
  repository writes already run lifecycle hooks; bare-pool writes do not provide
  equivalent transaction/event context. Neither is implicit request authority.
- Keep semantic actions for provider imports, acquisition, matching, file/device
  operations, backups and authentication. Verify the real actor and target owner
  before elevated internal work. Never choose an arbitrary user as a job owner.
- Queries are read-only. Metadata correction, reconnect/mount and other effects
  belong in explicit action mutations.
- Declare stored FK relations rather than handwritten relation resolvers.
  Review physical FK/delete semantics separately from virtual navigation.
  Mark upward propagation only on intended, bounded dependency edges; avoid cycles
  and shared-library fanout from personal playback checkpoints.
- Generated direct events are postcommit invalidations, not a durable replay log.
  Deleted children/old reparented parents need qualified surviving-parent updates.
  Do not handcraft change witnesses or raw broadcasts to evade authorization.
- Frontend domain documents live in `.graphql` sources and use schema codegen.
  Active views register scoped dependencies and snapshot reconciliation. Preserve
  loaded windows and last-good snapshots, coalesce bursts, resynchronize after
  reconnect/lag, and clear stale-principal state. No recurring domain query polls
  without a documented temporary exception.

Inspect `docs/backend-alignment-plan.md` and its audit inventories when changing
these boundaries. Validate authorization, transaction/event and data-completeness
behavior; passing operation parsing alone does not qualify the running schema.
